# Q38 If two processes use the same name, are they the same meaning? (process names, current or former, used by more than one process: each is a different IRI with its own definition and parent; since core 2.4.0 no two processes share a preferred label, and the names they shared are kept as core:priorPreferredLabel, EPM-DEC-001-0105)
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>
PREFIX mod: <https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/>
PREFIX core: <https://w3id.org/lsc/ontology/modules/core/>
SELECT ?name (COUNT(DISTINCT ?process) AS ?processes) (COUNT(DISTINCT ?parent) AS ?parents) WHERE {
  ?process skos:inScheme mod:core ; skos:broader ?parent .
  { ?process skos:prefLabel ?label } UNION { ?process core:priorPreferredLabel ?label }
  BIND(STR(?label) AS ?name)
} GROUP BY ?name HAVING (COUNT(DISTINCT ?process) > 1)
